ipv6: exthdrs: refresh nh pointer after ipv6_hop_jumbo()

jira KERNEL-1731
cve CVE-2026-63924
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-687.56.1.el9_8
commit-author Justin Iurman <justin.iurman@gmail.com>
commit d47548a36639095939f4747d4c43f2271366f565
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-687.56.1.el9_8/d47548a3.failed

ipv6_hop_jumbo() calls pskb_trim_rcsum(), which can change skb pointers.
Let's recompute nh pointer to make sure any change won't mess things up.

Fixes: 1da177e4c3f4 ("Linux-2.6.12-rc2")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Signed-off-by: Justin Iurman <justin.iurman@gmail.com>
	Reviewed-by: Ido Schimmel <idosch@nvidia.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260522112013.12342-1-justin.iurman@gmail.com
	Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit d47548a36639095939f4747d4c43f2271366f565)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

